#import "src.typ": *

#idx("Ejection")Ejection is the last procedure: the seat (@canopy-seat) takes the pilot out of a jet that cannot be landed.

=== When <ejection-when>

Eject when the jet is out of control and not recovering, when a fire goes on, when the engine has failed with no runway in reach (not below 2,000 ft above the ground unless a landing is sure#fm[section III, "Airstarts", page 3-79]; out of control, by 6,000 ft above the ground#fm[section III, "Ejection", the warnings, page 3-40]), or when a landing with damage would be worse. Decide early. Eject at the lowest speed practical#fm[section III, "Ejection", page 3-40]: the wind blast is moderate up to 400 kt, causes injuries from 400 to 600 kt and is beyond the body above 600 kt#fm[section III, "Ejection", the warnings, page 3-41].

=== How <ejection-how>

*At once:* pull the ejection handle.

*With time*#fm[section III, "Ejection (time permitting)", page 3-41]:

+ Come down from high altitude, and point the jet away from people.
+ IFF MASTER knob to EMER.
+ Stow loose things; tighten the lap belt and the chin strap; take off night-vision goggles.
+ Sit with the head on the headrest, the back and hips against the seat, the feet on the pedals.
+ Pull the handle.

If the canopy does not go, it is jettisoned by its own handle; if the seat does not fire after the canopy has gone, there is no other way out#fm[section III, "Ejection seat failure", page 3-43].

#in-sim[
  - #key("Eject (press 3 times)"): three presses, each within a second of the one before. #sym.arrow.r *The canopy goes, the seat fires and the parachute opens.* The engine stops and the controls are dead.
  - The height and the speed at ejection make no difference in the sim: the seat works from any height. The handle between the knees is not the control: the key is.
]
